      },
      "message": "feat(app): multi-seat indexable cutters take their whole record from the document\n\nA component row now holds the cutter facts of a multi-seat body\n(`milling`) and an insert's tool material and cutting rows (`running`).\n`tool_assembly::derive` gives a tool whose insert sits on such a body\nthe whole milling record of the #4192 resolver (flutes, flute length,\ncentre cutting, the enclosed holder; every seat checked). The insert's\nrunning data goes on each tool that cuts with it. `with_row` on the\nupsert and edit commands takes the whole row; an edit of the shared\ninsert updates every tool in one undo step, and the operations go\nStale by their stamps.\n\nRefs #3646\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
